ukui-settings-daemon (media-keys): handle the "blank" power-key action

The hardware power key is handled by the media-keys plugin of ukui-settings-daemon.
MediaKeyAction::doPowerKeyAction() reads the org.ukui.power-manager button-power
enum index and calls doSessionAction(PowerType).  PowerType (media-type.h) only
defines { POWER_SUSPEND=1, POWER_SHUTDOWN=2, POWER_HIBERNATE=3,
POWER_INTER_ACTIVE=4 } — there is no index 0 entry, so the value "blank"
(enum index 0) matches no case in doSessionAction()'s switch and falls through to
executeCommand("ukui-session-tools", {}) — i.e. it just shows the session menu,
so selecting "关闭显示器" did nothing but re-open the "询问" dialog.

This is the equivalent SOURCE change for making "blank" turn the panel off/on.
(The shipped fix, tools/sheng-power-button-blank-fix.sh, instead repoints the
"ukui-session-tools" program string in the compiled libmedia-keys.so to the
"ukui-session-tools"->"sheng-pwrkey" wrapper, so no rebuild is needed.)

--- a/plugins/media-keys/media-type.h
+++ b/plugins/media-keys/media-type.h
@@ -55,6 +55,7 @@ typedef enum {
 typedef enum {
+    POWER_BLANK = 0,
     POWER_SUSPEND = 1,
     POWER_SHUTDOWN,
     POWER_HIBERNATE,
     POWER_INTER_ACTIVE,
 }PowerType;
--- a/plugins/media-keys/media-key-action.cpp
+++ b/plugins/media-keys/media-key-action.cpp
@@ - (doPowerKeyAction)
     PowerType buttonType = POWER_INTER_ACTIVE;
     if (value.isValid()) {
         buttonType = (PowerType)value.toInt();
     } else {
         USD_LOG(LOG_WARNING, "get power key state is null");
     }
+    if (buttonType == POWER_BLANK) {
+        // sheng: 关闭/打开显示器
+        executeCommand("kscreen-doctor", QStringList({"-d", "off"}));
+        return;
+    }
     doSessionAction(buttonType);
